WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.780 --> 00:00:01.970
We have a new doc.

00:00:01.970 --> 00:00:07.950
You mean from the Trump FEMA and the Trump
CDC?

00:00:07.950 --> 00:00:15.789
And it predicts that by June 1st, we may see
3000 corona virus deaths per day.

00:00:15.789 --> 00:00:21.380
This is the exact opposite of the prevailing
narrative from the Trump administration.

00:00:21.380 --> 00:00:25.810
The prevailing narrative is deaths peaked
in mid-April at about twenty five hundred

00:00:25.810 --> 00:00:26.900
a day.

00:00:26.900 --> 00:00:30.240
They have been coming down and they will continue
to come down.

00:00:30.240 --> 00:00:32.119
So we should start reopening.

00:00:32.119 --> 00:00:38.239
That's a big difference than what FEMA and
the CDC say, which is by June 1st, the U.S.

00:00:38.239 --> 00:00:44.070
alone will see 200000 new cases a day and
3000 deaths per day.

00:00:44.070 --> 00:00:45.280
How could there be such a conflict?

00:00:45.280 --> 00:00:47.020
Well, we're going to figure that out.

00:00:47.020 --> 00:00:51.730
You all know I have not been playing politics
with Corona virus from day one.

00:00:51.730 --> 00:00:54.460
I have no interest in playing politics with
it.

00:00:54.460 --> 00:00:59.019
I hope that Donald Trump gets deaths down
to zero like that.

00:00:59.019 --> 00:01:03.719
And I have no concerns about the political
implications of that.

00:01:03.719 --> 00:01:06.040
I want to see the deaths reduced right away.

00:01:06.040 --> 00:01:10.100
I hope Trump is right here and the CDC and
FEMA are wrong.

00:01:10.100 --> 00:01:11.580
When we look at the headlines.

00:01:11.580 --> 00:01:20.200
So far, cases have been sort of pretty steadily
around 25000 new cases a day since the first

00:01:20.200 --> 00:01:21.780
days of April.

00:01:21.780 --> 00:01:26.399
We're testing about three times as much now
as we were a month ago.

00:01:26.399 --> 00:01:33.039
So if we keep finding 25000 new cases a day,
but we triple testing, that implies that we

00:01:33.039 --> 00:01:37.030
are starting to be on the tail end to some
degree when we look at deaths.

00:01:37.030 --> 00:01:42.119
We saw what looks like a peak in deaths around
April 20th, around twenty five hundred deaths

00:01:42.119 --> 00:01:44.470
a day, although it's been pretty up and down.

00:01:44.470 --> 00:01:48.670
One would imagine one would hope that deaths
are going to keep coming down, not go back

00:01:48.670 --> 00:01:50.360
up to 3000 a day.

00:01:50.360 --> 00:01:55.579
Twenty five days from now, when presented
with these documents from FEMA and the CDC,

00:01:55.579 --> 00:02:01.020
the Trump administration so far has simply
said these are real documents, but they have

00:02:01.020 --> 00:02:03.820
not been presented to the White House Corona
Virus Task Force.

00:02:03.820 --> 00:02:05.109
We've not evaluated them.

00:02:05.109 --> 00:02:10.890
We are not in a position to say that CDC and
FEMA are right now what would be a reason

00:02:10.890 --> 00:02:14.540
why we would see the numbers seemingly coming
down.

00:02:14.540 --> 00:02:17.099
But then go all the way back up later this
month.

00:02:17.099 --> 00:02:19.250
Sadly, the answer is something very basic.

00:02:19.250 --> 00:02:22.050
The early hot spots seem to be past their
peak.

00:02:22.050 --> 00:02:26.450
New York, here in Massachusetts, we had only
1.3 percent case growth yesterday.

00:02:26.450 --> 00:02:27.950
New Jersey.

00:02:27.950 --> 00:02:36.450
But the places that did not have an early
increase in early breakout outbreak, they

00:02:36.450 --> 00:02:40.040
are increasingly on a trajectory to become
hot spots.

00:02:40.040 --> 00:02:41.430
That's what viral growth is.

00:02:41.430 --> 00:02:46.100
When you look at Florida, for example, bragging
for weeks and weeks that they're they're fine.

00:02:46.100 --> 00:02:53.599
They're good to reopen 615 new cases in Florida
on Sunday, more than eight or nine hundred

00:02:53.599 --> 00:02:56.260
yesterday in 14 days.

00:02:56.260 --> 00:03:02.590
If that trajectory continues, Florida will
be a hub of coronavirus in the United States,

00:03:02.590 --> 00:03:03.590
Georgia.

00:03:03.590 --> 00:03:06.610
Georgia had three hundred and thirty nine
new cases on Sunday.

00:03:06.610 --> 00:03:08.480
On Monday, they had more than double that.

00:03:08.480 --> 00:03:11.370
If that trajectory continues, Georgia's in
trouble.

00:03:11.370 --> 00:03:14.760
Louisiana, very big increase from Sunday to
Monday.

00:03:14.760 --> 00:03:16.069
So the numbers are still small.

00:03:16.069 --> 00:03:20.209
You're talking about hundreds of cases a day,
not thousands or tens of thousands.

00:03:20.209 --> 00:03:25.310
But look at the percentage increases and extrapolate
out 10, 15 days.

00:03:25.310 --> 00:03:28.629
Those will be massive death zones if that
happens.

00:03:28.629 --> 00:03:35.629
Now, if we get to 3000 deaths per day around
June 1st, we are going to blow the 100000

00:03:35.629 --> 00:03:39.189
person death toll out of the water very, very
quickly.

00:03:39.189 --> 00:03:43.230
Just 10 days of 3000 a day is 30k.

00:03:43.230 --> 00:03:48.030
If we go from where we are now to 3000 in
the next twenty five days.

00:03:48.030 --> 00:03:49.430
That's another 50000 deaths.

00:03:49.430 --> 00:03:55.549
So if this estimate is correct, by mid-June
we would be at one hundred and fifty thousand

00:03:55.549 --> 00:03:58.209
deaths and we would just be getting started.

00:03:58.209 --> 00:04:00.590
I hope that this is not accurate.

00:04:00.590 --> 00:04:01.969
That would be a daily 9/11.

00:04:01.969 --> 00:04:08.849
What I fear the most is that the Trump administration
knows that they've failed and they are not

00:04:08.849 --> 00:04:13.579
going to even address these new concerns from
CDC and FEMA that they're not even going to

00:04:13.579 --> 00:04:19.000
try and they're just going to do propaganda
and economic messages from here on out while

00:04:19.000 --> 00:04:22.440
shifting the blame for the deaths to governors.

00:04:22.440 --> 00:04:24.780
I wish I could say that that wasn't going
to work.

00:04:24.780 --> 00:04:26.470
But unfortunately, it may.

00:04:26.470 --> 00:04:27.780
They're not beating it.

00:04:27.780 --> 00:04:29.830
They're not protecting Americans.

00:04:29.830 --> 00:04:36.850
But what they have shown they can do effectively
is shift blame and distract and now say, listen,

00:04:36.850 --> 00:04:37.850
we did our part.

00:04:37.850 --> 00:04:40.180
We're now doing the economic stuff.

00:04:40.180 --> 00:04:41.940
These governors aren't testing enough.

00:04:41.940 --> 00:04:44.290
These governors aren't making the right decisions.

00:04:44.290 --> 00:04:46.450
These governors haven't secured PPE.

00:04:46.450 --> 00:04:47.450
It's on them now.

00:04:47.450 --> 00:04:48.450
I hope it doesn't work.

00:04:48.450 --> 00:04:50.880
I hope this death toll doesn't even happen.

00:04:50.880 --> 00:04:53.729
But this is what CDC and FEMA are now predicting.

00:04:53.729 --> 00:04:55.000
Let me know what you think.

00:04:55.000 --> 00:04:56.280
Check out the reports.

00:04:56.280 --> 00:05:00.419
Check out the papers and let me know on Twitter
at David Pakman.

